---
const federationNodes = [
  { x: 36, y: 66, w: 240, h: 84, title: 'Origin Key Service', lines: ['Lease includes the Target', 'Non-Captive material + FLP'], kind: 'key' },
  { x: 36, y: 218, w: 240, h: 76, title: 'Publishing application', lines: ['Encrypts the report locally'], kind: 'plain' },
  { x: 326, y: 208, w: 180, h: 96, title: 'Shared delivery', lines: ['Envelope + inline FLP', 'No report decryption key'], kind: 'plain' },
  { x: 556, y: 66, w: 308, h: 84, title: 'Target Key Service', lines: ['Has federation private material', 'Verifies FLP; applies local policy'], kind: 'key' },
  { x: 556, y: 218, w: 308, h: 76, title: 'Receiving application', lines: ['Delivered Envelope + FLP'], kind: 'plain' },
];
const availabilityNodes = [
  { x: 48, y: 84, w: 244, h: 88, title: 'Key Server A', lines: ['Unavailable'], kind: 'unavailable' },
  { x: 332, y: 84, w: 234, h: 88, title: 'Durable recoverability', lines: ['Implementation-neutral', 'Required state remains available'], kind: 'state' },
  { x: 606, y: 84, w: 244, h: 88, title: 'Key Server B', lines: ['Handles the fresh request', 'Policy permits this reader'], kind: 'key' },
  { x: 320, y: 278, w: 260, h: 90, title: 'Receiving application', lines: ['Quotes Lease Reference + FLP', 'Decrypts the report locally'], kind: 'plain' },
];
---
<figure class="fha-figure" aria-labelledby="fha-caption">
  <div class="fha-heading"><strong>Two views of the same receiving arrangement</strong><span>Architectural example</span></div>
  <div class="fha-view">
    <h3>A. Federation between Domains</h3>
    <div class="fha-desktop">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 900 366" role="img" aria-labelledby="fha-federation-title fha-federation-desc">
        <title id="fha-federation-title">A prepared Target Domain services local key access after the Origin connection fails</title>
        <desc id="fha-federation-desc">The Origin Key Service supplies a Non-Captive Lease and FLP to the publisher. The publisher encrypts locally. Shared delivery carries the Envelope and FLP to the Target application. After delivery the Origin connection is unavailable. A fresh local key request reaches the Target Key Service, which has the federation private material, verifies the FLP and applies policy.</desc>
        <defs>
          <marker id="fha-data-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" fill="#68717c" /></marker>
          <marker id="fha-federation-key-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" fill="#265f99" /></marker>
        </defs>
        <rect class="fha-domain" x="16" y="16" width="280" height="300" rx="8" />
        <rect class="fha-domain" x="536" y="16" width="348" height="300" rx="8" />
        <text class="fha-domain-label" x="36" y="44">Origin CABE Domain</text>
        <text class="fha-domain-label" x="556" y="44">Target CABE Domain</text>
        <path class="fha-edge key" d="M156 150 V218" marker-start="url(#fha-federation-key-arrow)" marker-end="url(#fha-federation-key-arrow)" />
        <text class="fha-label" x="170" y="188">Lease + FLP</text>
        <path class="fha-edge key" d="M710 150 V218" marker-start="url(#fha-federation-key-arrow)" marker-end="url(#fha-federation-key-arrow)" />
        <text class="fha-label" x="724" y="180">Fresh local request</text>
        <text class="fha-label" x="724" y="198">Permitted material</text>
        <path class="fha-edge plain" d="M276 256 H326" marker-end="url(#fha-data-arrow)" />
        <path class="fha-edge plain" d="M506 256 H556" marker-end="url(#fha-data-arrow)" />
        <rect x="295" y="244" width="20" height="24" fill="white" />
        <path class="fha-break" d="M298 246 L312 266 M312 246 L298 266" />
        <text class="fha-outage-label" x="36" y="347">× Origin connection unavailable after delivery</text>
        {federationNodes.map(node => <g class={`fha-node ${node.kind}`}>
          <rect x={node.x} y={node.y} width={node.w} height={node.h} rx="6" />
          <text class="fha-node-title" x={node.x + 14} y={node.y + 26}>{node.title}</text>
          {node.lines.map((line, i) => <text class="fha-node-copy" x={node.x + 14} y={node.y + 49 + i * 20}>{line}</text>)}
        </g>)}
      </svg>
    </div>
    <ol class="fha-mobile">
      <li><strong>Origin Domain</strong><p>The publisher obtains a Non-Captive Lease and an FLP for the prepared Target, then encrypts the report locally.</p></li>
      <li><strong>Shared delivery</strong><p>The Envelope and inline FLP reach the Target application. The Origin connection then fails.</p></li>
      <li class="key"><strong>Target Domain</strong><p>A fresh local request quotes the FLP. The Key Service recovers material, verifies the request and applies local policy.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <div class="fha-view">
    <h3>B. High availability within the Target Domain</h3>
    <div class="fha-desktop">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 900 414" role="img" aria-labelledby="fha-ha-title fha-ha-desc">
        <title id="fha-ha-title">Two Key Servers implement one logical Target Key Service</title>
        <desc id="fha-ha-desc">Key Server A is unavailable. Required durable recovery state remains available through implementation-neutral arrangements within this Domain. The receiving application makes a fresh request to Key Server B with the Lease Reference and FLP. Server B verifies the package and evaluates access; the permitted application obtains the material and decrypts locally. The dotted lines express state dependencies, not a prescribed storage topology.</desc>
        <defs>
          <marker id="fha-ha-key-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" fill="#265f99" /></marker>
        </defs>
        <rect class="fha-domain" x="16" y="16" width="868" height="382" rx="8" />
        <text class="fha-domain-label" x="36" y="45">Target CABE Domain · one logical Key Service</text>
        <path class="fha-edge state" d="M292 128 H332 M566 128 H606" />
        <path class="fha-edge key" d="M728 172 V323 H580" marker-start="url(#fha-ha-key-arrow)" marker-end="url(#fha-ha-key-arrow)" />
        <text class="fha-label" x="744" y="235">Fresh request + FLP</text>
        <text class="fha-label" x="744" y="256">Permitted material</text>
        <text class="fha-label" x="449" y="211" text-anchor="middle">Recovery arrangements are local to this Domain.</text>
        <text class="fha-label" x="449" y="231" text-anchor="middle">No storage or replication topology is prescribed.</text>
        {availabilityNodes.map(node => <g class={`fha-node ${node.kind}`}>
          <rect x={node.x} y={node.y} width={node.w} height={node.h} rx="6" />
          <text class="fha-node-title" x={node.x + 14} y={node.y + 26}>{node.title}</text>
          {node.lines.map((line, i) => <text class="fha-node-copy" x={node.x + 14} y={node.y + 49 + i * 20}>{line}</text>)}
        </g>)}
        <path class="fha-break" d="M255 101 L271 117 M271 101 L255 117" />
      </svg>
    </div>
    <ol class="fha-mobile">
      <li class="unavailable"><strong>Target Key Server A fails</strong><p>The Target still has the required durable recovery state and local dependencies.</p></li>
      <li class="key"><strong>Target Key Server B handles the request</strong><p>The reader quotes the Lease Reference and FLP in a fresh request. Permitted material enables local decryption.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <ul class="fha-legend" aria-label="Diagram line types">
    <li><span class="plain"></span>Encrypted delivery</li>
    <li><span class="key"></span>Key request / response</li>
    <li><span class="state"></span>State dependency · implementation-neutral</li>
  </ul>
  <figcaption id="fha-caption">View A shows the prepared exchange after delivery; View B expands the Target Key Service during a server failure. The report stays at the applications. Continuity depends on available material, durable recovery arrangements and local services.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .fha-figure { margin-block: 28px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; background: white; }
  .fha-heading { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 20px; justify-content: space-between; padding: 18px 20px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .fha-heading strong { font-size: 14px; }
  .fha-heading span { font-size: 11px; color: var(--quiet); }
  .fha-view { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 16px; }
  .fha-view h3 { margin: 0 20px 10px; font-size: 14px; }
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .fha-domain { fill: #fafbfc; stroke: var(--line); stroke-dasharray: 5 5; }
  .fha-domain-label { font: 600 13px var(--font-body); fill: var(--muted); }
  .fha-node rect { fill: white; stroke: #ccd3dc; }
  .fha-node.key rect { fill: var(--blue-soft); stroke: var(--blue-line); }
  .fha-node.state rect { fill: #fbf9f5; stroke: #c8b496; }
  .fha-node.unavailable rect { fill: #fcf7f7; stroke: #d9b3b3; }
  .fha-node-title { font: 600 14px var(--font-body); fill: var(--ink); }
  .fha-node-copy { font: 13px var(--font-body); fill: var(--muted); }
  .fha-node.unavailable .fha-node-copy { fill: var(--deny); }
  .fha-edge { fill: none; stroke-width: 2; }
  .fha-edge.plain { stroke: var(--quiet); }
  .fha-edge.key { stroke: var(--blue); stroke-dasharray: 7 4; }
  .fha-edge.state { stroke: #80633e; stroke-dasharray: 2 4; }
  .fha-label { fill: var(--muted); font: 12px var(--font-body); }
  .fha-outage-label { fill: var(--deny); font: 12px var(--font-body); }
  .fha-break { fill: none; stroke: var(--deny); stroke-width: 2.5; }
  .fha-legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 20px; list-style: none; padding: 12px 20px; margin: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .fha-legend li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: 11px; margin: 0; }
  .fha-legend span { width: 24px; border-top: 2px solid var(--quiet); }
  .fha-legend .key { border-color: var(--blue); border-top-style: dashed; }
  .fha-legend .state { border-color: #80633e; border-top-style: dotted; }
  figcaption { padding: 16px 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--soft); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.75; }
  .fha-mobile { display: none; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .fha-desktop, .fha-legend { display: none; }
    .fha-mobile { display: grid; gap: 16px; list-style: none; padding: 10px 20px 20px; margin: 0; }
    .fha-mobile li { margin: 0; padding-left: 13px; border-left: 2px solid var(--quiet); }
    .fha-mobile li.key { border-color: var(--blue); border-left-style: dashed; }
    .fha-mobile li.unavailable { border-color: var(--deny); }
    .fha-mobile strong { font-size: 14px; }
    .fha-mobile p { margin-top: 7px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.8; }
  }
  @media print { .fha-view { break-inside: avoid; } }
</style>
